1
00:00:50,049 --> 00:00:53,219
THE ORDINARY JACKPOT

2
00:01:05,648 --> 00:01:08,484
<i>Sometimes, I get so caught up working</i>

3
00:01:08,568 --> 00:01:10,653
<i>and end up alone in the office.</i>

4
00:01:12,363 --> 00:01:13,781
<i>When that happens</i>

5
00:01:13,864 --> 00:01:16,284
<i>part of me wants to leave</i>
<i>as soon as I can</i>

6
00:01:17,785 --> 00:01:19,579
<i>while another part of me</i>

7
00:01:20,246 --> 00:01:21,664
<i>feels proud of working hard.</i>

8
00:01:23,124 --> 00:01:26,252
<i>I even fool myself into thinking</i>

9
00:01:26,335 --> 00:01:28,004
<i>I'm the most important person</i>
<i>in the company.</i>

10
00:01:31,591 --> 00:01:34,051
<i>I have 1.3 billion won.</i>

11
00:01:35,094 --> 00:01:39,056
<i>But that's not enough to quit my job</i>
<i>or completely change my life.</i>

12
00:01:40,975 --> 00:01:44,770
<i>I can't decide what to do</i>
<i>with the money.</i>

13
00:01:45,229 --> 00:01:47,940
<i>So I continue going to work.</i>

14
00:01:55,990 --> 00:01:59,744
<i>In the meantime,</i>
<i>while I'm stuck in indecision...</i>

15
00:02:01,746 --> 00:02:05,499
<i>someone else is taking</i>
<i>the biggest leap of their life.</i>

16
00:02:31,359 --> 00:02:33,444
RESIGNATION LETTER
JEONG SEON-HYUK

17
00:02:34,570 --> 00:02:38,324
If you want a raise or more benefits,
or if the work is too tough

18
00:02:38,991 --> 00:02:41,410
just say so
instead of pulling a stunt like this.

19
00:02:42,870 --> 00:02:45,623
It's not that.
I'm really planning to leave.

20
00:02:46,916 --> 00:02:49,418
Isn't your kid starting school soon?
Can you afford to quit?

21
00:02:49,877 --> 00:02:52,338
Yes, we'll be fine for now.

22
00:02:54,423 --> 00:02:56,300
What brought this on all of a sudden?

23
00:02:56,634 --> 00:02:59,261
Honestly, didn't you
see this coming, Ms. Park?

24
00:02:59,804 --> 00:03:01,055
If I try to make a move

25
00:03:01,138 --> 00:03:04,016
it feels like I'm getting in the way
of the others' promotions.

26
00:03:04,642 --> 00:03:06,352
But if I do nothing

27
00:03:06,435 --> 00:03:09,063
it feels like I'm holding back
the newer, younger employees.

28
00:03:10,773 --> 00:03:12,983
Mr. Jeong, you are so...

29
00:03:13,067 --> 00:03:14,235
Pathetic, aren't I?

30
00:03:14,485 --> 00:03:15,695
Trust me, I know.

31
00:03:16,278 --> 00:03:17,405
I know that

32
00:03:18,239 --> 00:03:20,741
but once I took a passive approach

33
00:03:20,825 --> 00:03:23,077
it was hard to break out of it.

34
00:03:23,869 --> 00:03:26,997
So I'm trying to change
my environment instead.

35
00:03:29,083 --> 00:03:30,126
Starting your own business?

36
00:03:34,088 --> 00:03:36,674
I won't make you sign
a non-compete agreement

37
00:03:37,091 --> 00:03:38,175
so be honest with me.

38
00:03:49,812 --> 00:03:56,068
EPISODE 4:
MUTUAL CAUSE, MUTUAL EFFECT

39
00:03:58,738 --> 00:04:00,573
- Hello, Ju-hui.
- Hello.

40
00:04:01,866 --> 00:04:03,492
Come on, get to work on time.

41
00:04:03,576 --> 00:04:04,702
A team leader shouldn't be last.

42
00:04:05,453 --> 00:04:07,079
Right, my apologies.

43
00:04:07,163 --> 00:04:09,039
You've been
exactly 13 minutes late lately.

44
00:04:09,123 --> 00:04:10,124
Going to the gym?

45
00:04:10,458 --> 00:04:12,084
I had something to take care of.

46
00:04:15,129 --> 00:04:16,422
We all have our own things going on.

47
00:04:17,381 --> 00:04:20,176
That's an excuse for a rookie,
not a team leader.

48
00:04:22,261 --> 00:04:23,262
I'm sorry.

49
00:04:28,851 --> 00:04:30,102
And where's Mr. Jeong?

50
00:04:31,145 --> 00:04:33,439
Even if he's quitting,
he should still get here on time.

51
00:04:34,106 --> 00:04:35,399
Isn't that common courtesy?

52
00:04:35,483 --> 00:04:37,485
He said he was going
to stop by the mall today

53
00:04:37,568 --> 00:04:39,278
to say his goodbyes.

54
00:04:40,780 --> 00:04:43,073
Everyone's just doing
whatever they want.

55
00:04:43,741 --> 00:04:45,659
Is this a playground?
A train station?

56
00:04:48,829 --> 00:04:50,456
How ridiculous.

57
00:04:56,378 --> 00:04:58,005
All right, let's start the meeting.

58
00:04:58,088 --> 00:04:59,340
We have a lot to go over.

59
00:05:01,425 --> 00:05:02,885
Gi-tae, when are you going
to the mall?

60
00:05:02,968 --> 00:05:04,428
I'll head over right after lunch.

61
00:05:04,512 --> 00:05:06,514
They need to finish construction
this week

62
00:05:06,597 --> 00:05:08,265
so keep morale up,
but keep the pressure on too.

63
00:05:08,349 --> 00:05:09,350
Got it.

64
00:05:09,433 --> 00:05:11,769
Also, tonight at 8 p.m.

65
00:05:12,311 --> 00:05:13,312
You remember, correct?

66
00:05:13,604 --> 00:05:14,605
Yes.

67
00:05:17,691 --> 00:05:19,193
6TH FLOOR SALES DIVISION 1

68
00:05:23,614 --> 00:05:27,076
Assistant Manager Jang Hyang-eun
will join our team next week.

69
00:05:28,077 --> 00:05:29,078
But she's already here.

70
00:05:29,495 --> 00:05:30,496
Pardon?

71
00:05:31,872 --> 00:05:32,873
Hello, Mr. Gong.

72
00:05:34,917 --> 00:05:36,710
Oh, hello, Ms. Jang.

73
00:05:37,711 --> 00:05:39,338
What brings you here?

74
00:05:39,421 --> 00:05:42,383
I came to say hello
and meet our business partners.

75
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:44,093
Have you been well?

76
00:05:44,176 --> 00:05:45,511
Yes, it's been a long time.

77
00:05:45,761 --> 00:05:46,762
Right.

78
00:05:47,429 --> 00:05:48,430
Hello, Mr. Yang.

79
00:05:48,681 --> 00:05:51,183
Wow, long time no see.
I look forward to working with you.

80
00:05:51,851 --> 00:05:53,060
Likewise.

81
00:05:53,143 --> 00:05:55,312
You haven't met these two yet,
have you?

82
00:05:55,396 --> 00:05:57,231
- This is...
- Gi-tae?

83
00:05:57,314 --> 00:05:58,440
Hello, ma'am.

84
00:05:58,983 --> 00:06:00,025
I've heard a lot about you.

85
00:06:00,568 --> 00:06:02,069
All good things, I hope.

86
00:06:02,653 --> 00:06:03,779
Yes, of course.

87
00:06:04,947 --> 00:06:05,948
And you're Ji-hye?

88
00:06:06,031 --> 00:06:07,992
I look forward
to working with you, ma'am.

89
00:06:08,242 --> 00:06:10,744
- Are you managing the center?
- Yes.

90
00:06:10,828 --> 00:06:12,329
Can I ask you a favor?

91
00:06:12,413 --> 00:06:13,873
Of course, anything.

92
00:06:13,956 --> 00:06:16,333
I'd like the following information
by my first official day.

93
00:06:16,417 --> 00:06:19,044
Baseline margins for the brands
Team 5 is in charge of.

94
00:06:19,128 --> 00:06:20,337
Customer prices.

95
00:06:20,421 --> 00:06:22,047
Each brand's customer service manual.

96
00:06:22,131 --> 00:06:23,340
Credit memo logs.

97
00:06:23,424 --> 00:06:24,592
Invoice checklists.

98
00:06:24,675 --> 00:06:26,260
Total penalty points.

99
00:06:26,343 --> 00:06:29,054
Direct numbers for all brand reps
as well as their email addresses.

100
00:06:29,513 --> 00:06:31,348
Can you put that together for me?

101
00:06:34,393 --> 00:06:37,104
Baseline margins, customer prices...

102
00:06:37,354 --> 00:06:38,564
Customer service manuals.

103
00:06:38,647 --> 00:06:40,149
I'd be disappointed
if I had to repeat myself.

104
00:06:42,610 --> 00:06:44,570
I'll say hello to Ms. Park.

105
00:06:50,284 --> 00:06:51,285
That's Ms. Jang.

106
00:06:52,244 --> 00:06:53,662
She was always good at her job, no?

107
00:06:53,996 --> 00:06:55,289
She hasn't changed a bit.

108
00:06:55,831 --> 00:06:56,832
Is this right?

109
00:06:56,916 --> 00:06:58,375
Will Ji-hye and I be okay?

110
00:06:58,959 --> 00:07:00,419
Of course not.

111
00:07:00,502 --> 00:07:01,795
You're screwed.

112
00:07:01,879 --> 00:07:03,088
DAILY ROUTINE

113
00:07:03,172 --> 00:07:04,256
<i>Thank you.</i>

114
00:07:08,385 --> 00:07:10,638
I didn't know there was
a spot like this nearby.

115
00:07:10,721 --> 00:07:12,473
Most of our colleagues don't know.

116
00:07:12,556 --> 00:07:14,600
I stop by every morning before work.

117
00:07:15,142 --> 00:07:18,020
So you called me to ask
about Jang Hyang-eun, right?

118
00:07:18,437 --> 00:07:21,190
Yeah, she's joining my team,
so I need to know more about her.

119
00:07:21,273 --> 00:07:23,150
I told you all I know last time.

120
00:07:23,233 --> 00:07:25,277
Something happened
while she was at the China branch.

121
00:07:25,361 --> 00:07:28,364
But they kept a tight lid on it,
so no one knows the details.

122
00:07:29,073 --> 00:07:32,701
They froze all personnel transfers,
but she managed to return to Korea.

123
00:07:33,369 --> 00:07:34,370
That's everything.

124
00:07:34,578 --> 00:07:36,580
So you don't actually know anything.

125
00:07:36,997 --> 00:07:38,040
I don't.

126
00:07:38,832 --> 00:07:40,751
But nothing good will come
from getting involved with her.

127
00:07:40,834 --> 00:07:42,419
Whatever she did while she was there

128
00:07:42,503 --> 00:07:44,838
it'll only make it harder
to work with the China branch.

129
00:07:45,589 --> 00:07:46,799
All right, then.

130
00:07:46,882 --> 00:07:48,467
I'm sure she'll tell me
when she's ready.

131
00:07:49,426 --> 00:07:51,637
That's a good mindset.
Just take it easy.

132
00:07:52,137 --> 00:07:54,890
All you need to think about is
how to utilize your team members.

133
00:07:55,391 --> 00:07:57,309
Ms. Jang should take over
the center now.

134
00:07:58,811 --> 00:08:01,522
I said, think about it.
Really think it through.

135
00:08:05,275 --> 00:08:06,819
What about Lee Ji-hye?

136
00:08:07,194 --> 00:08:09,196
She's only a contract worker,
so she must be anxious already.

137
00:08:09,279 --> 00:08:11,907
And now this woman flies in
from China and takes her spot?

138
00:08:11,991 --> 00:08:13,534
How do you think she'd feel?

139
00:08:15,828 --> 00:08:17,246
Even so, work is work.

140
00:08:19,123 --> 00:08:21,041
You're so cold-blooded.

141
00:08:21,709 --> 00:08:23,794
Don't you have any empathy?

142
00:08:25,713 --> 00:08:26,964
What about you?

143
00:08:27,047 --> 00:08:29,341
You claim to be such an empath.

144
00:08:29,717 --> 00:08:31,635
But why don't you empathize with me?

145
00:08:32,261 --> 00:08:34,054
You sure have a way with words.

146
00:08:35,097 --> 00:08:38,183
Anyway, keep doing your job

147
00:08:38,892 --> 00:08:41,770
but don't forget to look out
for your team, Mr. Gong.

148
00:08:43,313 --> 00:08:44,606
I got this for you.

149
00:08:45,107 --> 00:08:47,651
Try it. It'll bring out your empathy.

150
00:08:55,993 --> 00:08:57,036
It's good.

151
00:08:57,119 --> 00:08:58,203
See, I told you.

152
00:09:05,544 --> 00:09:06,754
Hello, Mr. Yang.

153
00:09:07,046 --> 00:09:10,090
I just arrived at the store.

154
00:09:10,174 --> 00:09:11,967
Sure, I'll send you a photo.

155
00:09:12,051 --> 00:09:13,260
All right.

156
00:09:13,802 --> 00:09:15,763
VITAMIN ENERGY DRINK

157
00:09:25,230 --> 00:09:27,608
Hello, sir.
Thank you for your hard work.

158
00:09:27,691 --> 00:09:29,151
Hey, get off me.

159
00:09:29,234 --> 00:09:30,527
I'm already hot as it is.

160
00:09:31,445 --> 00:09:32,780
My goodness.

161
00:09:32,863 --> 00:09:34,782
Construction is practically done.

162
00:09:34,865 --> 00:09:35,866
Done, my foot.

163
00:09:35,949 --> 00:09:37,326
We've got a long way to go.

164
00:09:37,409 --> 00:09:39,453
We worked until 2 a.m. last night.

165
00:09:40,079 --> 00:09:42,456
Don't give us last-minute orders.

166
00:09:42,539 --> 00:09:44,249
You always cut it close.

167
00:09:46,001 --> 00:09:47,628
Come on now.

168
00:09:48,295 --> 00:09:50,172
Have a drink, sir.

169
00:09:50,255 --> 00:09:51,256
- Fine.
- All right.

170
00:09:53,050 --> 00:09:54,676
Have a drink while you work.

171
00:09:56,095 --> 00:09:57,930
Here you go.
Thank you for your hard work.

172
00:10:00,224 --> 00:10:02,893
Gosh, it's so dusty in here.

173
00:10:03,560 --> 00:10:04,978
This just won't do.

174
00:10:06,772 --> 00:10:08,398
Hi, is this General Affairs?

175
00:10:08,482 --> 00:10:10,192
I'm calling from the Laknes store.

176
00:10:10,275 --> 00:10:11,902
Can you send someone to vacuum?

177
00:10:12,569 --> 00:10:13,570
Sorry?

178
00:10:13,654 --> 00:10:17,199
You should know
where the Laknes store is by now.

179
00:10:17,825 --> 00:10:21,286
Do you have any idea
how hard these people are working?

180
00:10:22,037 --> 00:10:24,289
Yes, please be more considerate.

181
00:10:24,665 --> 00:10:26,750
Thank you in advance.

182
00:10:27,793 --> 00:10:29,336
- Jeez.
- Goodness.

183
00:10:29,419 --> 00:10:31,338
You Hongsung people, I swear...

184
00:10:31,797 --> 00:10:34,258
So should we start
the electrical work?

185
00:10:34,967 --> 00:10:35,968
You're the best.

186
00:10:36,552 --> 00:10:38,345
We're counting on you.

187
00:10:38,428 --> 00:10:39,429
Whatever.

188
00:10:40,305 --> 00:10:41,849
Let's start on electrical.

189
00:10:41,932 --> 00:10:43,058
We can follow the blueprint.

190
00:10:43,142 --> 00:10:44,852
All right, let's see.

191
00:10:45,144 --> 00:10:47,020
Since this is a clothing store...

192
00:10:47,104 --> 00:10:50,107
- These aren't heavy at all.
- Just leave them. We'll handle it.

193
00:10:50,190 --> 00:10:52,025
It's the least I can do.

194
00:10:52,401 --> 00:10:53,485
Light as a feather.

195
00:11:15,757 --> 00:11:17,926
- Hey, Gi-tae.
<i>- Hello, Mr. Yang.</i>

196
00:11:18,010 --> 00:11:19,553
<i>Construction is going well.</i>

197
00:11:19,636 --> 00:11:21,096
They're cleaning up now.

198
00:11:21,180 --> 00:11:23,390
<i>Okay, good work.</i>
<i>Are you coming back now?</i>

199
00:11:23,473 --> 00:11:25,893
Oh, since I'm here

200
00:11:25,976 --> 00:11:28,478
I figured I'd make my rounds
at the other stores.

201
00:11:28,562 --> 00:11:30,898
Good idea. But don't go empty-handed.

202
00:11:30,981 --> 00:11:32,649
<i>Buy them something to drink.</i>

203
00:11:32,733 --> 00:11:34,735
Understood, sir.

204
00:11:34,818 --> 00:11:36,904
I'll see you later, then.

205
00:11:36,987 --> 00:11:38,405
All right. Good work.

206
00:11:40,991 --> 00:11:42,701
Gi-tae's gotten pretty savvy.

207
00:11:43,911 --> 00:11:46,205
- It looks too cramped, doesn't it?
- Yes.

208
00:11:46,705 --> 00:11:48,165
It might fall off the edge.

209
00:11:49,333 --> 00:11:51,710
How about this...

210
00:11:52,961 --> 00:11:54,087
I think it's okay now.

211
00:11:59,218 --> 00:12:00,969
Over here, Mr. Jeong.

212
00:12:07,392 --> 00:12:09,102
Were you checking on construction?

213
00:12:10,437 --> 00:12:11,438
Yes.

214
00:12:20,864 --> 00:12:21,865
Have a seat.

215
00:12:32,251 --> 00:12:33,919
Did you make your rounds?

216
00:12:34,294 --> 00:12:37,381
Yes, I said hello
to everyone at the office.

217
00:12:37,673 --> 00:12:39,299
How does it feel to be back?

218
00:12:40,926 --> 00:12:42,261
It's great, of course.

219
00:12:42,928 --> 00:12:44,263
A bit awkward too.

220
00:12:45,639 --> 00:12:46,890
You must have a lot on your mind.

221
00:12:48,392 --> 00:12:50,269
I'm not entirely at ease.

222
00:12:52,020 --> 00:12:53,772
It wasn't an easy decision
for me, either.

223
00:12:54,815 --> 00:12:57,526
I wasn't sure taking you in
was the right call.

224
00:12:59,736 --> 00:13:02,197
I completely understand
where you're coming from.

225
00:13:02,281 --> 00:13:03,615
Let me be clear.

226
00:13:04,074 --> 00:13:06,451
Just because I approved it
doesn't mean I was happy about it.

227
00:13:07,869 --> 00:13:08,912
Yes, ma'am.

228
00:13:10,205 --> 00:13:13,041
The audit of the China branch
is starting now.

229
00:13:13,125 --> 00:13:16,169
Depending on the outcome,
it could turn into a criminal case.

230
00:13:16,253 --> 00:13:17,296
Are you aware of that?

231
00:13:17,796 --> 00:13:19,339
Yes, I'm aware.

232
00:13:19,423 --> 00:13:21,174
I can't help but wonder.

233
00:13:21,258 --> 00:13:23,885
All personnel transfers were frozen

234
00:13:24,511 --> 00:13:26,930
but how did just one person
transfer to Korea?

235
00:13:27,472 --> 00:13:28,473
On top of that

236
00:13:29,516 --> 00:13:31,935
I heard a complaint
was filed against you.

237
00:13:33,603 --> 00:13:36,523
Did you abandon a sinking ship
to save yourself?

238
00:13:41,903 --> 00:13:44,239
I don't know
if you can't say anything

239
00:13:44,323 --> 00:13:46,658
or if you're just choosing
to stay silent.

240
00:13:48,952 --> 00:13:50,370
But I think it's possible

241
00:13:50,454 --> 00:13:53,874
you're in league with the people
who embezzled from the China branch.

242
00:13:53,957 --> 00:13:54,958
But...

243
00:13:55,542 --> 00:13:58,211
We shouldn't assume anything
without evidence.

244
00:13:59,379 --> 00:14:00,922
That's why I took you in.

245
00:14:02,549 --> 00:14:03,550
Yes, ma'am.

246
00:14:04,509 --> 00:14:06,678
There's only one thing
you can do here.

247
00:14:08,847 --> 00:14:10,390
Work hard.

248
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:15,354
If the audit results are positive,
that's great news for you.

249
00:14:15,896 --> 00:14:17,564
And even if they're negative

250
00:14:18,065 --> 00:14:21,276
your hard work will still count
for something.

251
00:14:21,902 --> 00:14:23,362
Do you get what I'm saying?

252
00:14:24,029 --> 00:14:25,030
Yes, ma'am.

253
00:14:25,697 --> 00:14:27,491
All right, you may go.

254
00:14:29,785 --> 00:14:30,786
Yes, ma'am.

255
00:15:05,570 --> 00:15:08,740
2 MONTHS AGO, CHINA

256
00:15:10,659 --> 00:15:11,660
POINT OF CONTACT

257
00:15:11,743 --> 00:15:13,245
TRADING COMPANY TRANSACTIONS

258
00:15:26,925 --> 00:15:28,427
COPY TO USB DRIVE

259
00:15:30,512 --> 00:15:31,638
Who's there?

260
00:15:45,777 --> 00:15:47,571
CUSTOMER SERVICE MANUAL

261
00:15:47,654 --> 00:15:48,780
What are you working on?

262
00:15:50,365 --> 00:15:52,826
The documents Ms. Jang requested.

263
00:15:53,493 --> 00:15:54,995
Are you putting them together
like this?

264
00:15:56,288 --> 00:15:58,206
Is this not good enough?

265
00:15:59,833 --> 00:16:01,626
No, you're doing great.

266
00:16:01,918 --> 00:16:03,086
- Mr. Yang.
- Yes?

267
00:16:05,630 --> 00:16:06,923
Mr. Gong, it's time for lunch.

268
00:16:07,382 --> 00:16:08,675
Is it?

269
00:16:09,217 --> 00:16:10,218
Let's go.

270
00:16:10,844 --> 00:16:11,845
Come on, Ji-hye.

271
00:16:11,928 --> 00:16:14,014
I'm not really hungry.

272
00:16:14,306 --> 00:16:15,307
You two go ahead.

273
00:16:15,724 --> 00:16:17,893
How can you work on an empty stomach?

274
00:16:18,268 --> 00:16:19,769
Should I get you
a salad or something?

275
00:16:19,853 --> 00:16:21,438
No, I'll be fine.

276
00:16:21,521 --> 00:16:22,731
Enjoy your lunch.

277
00:16:28,111 --> 00:16:29,779
Mr. Jeong hasn't come in yet?

278
00:16:30,405 --> 00:16:32,032
No, and he's not answering his phone.

279
00:16:59,726 --> 00:17:01,311
- Hello.
- Hello.

280
00:17:01,394 --> 00:17:02,854
- Hello.
- Yes, hello.

281
00:17:02,938 --> 00:17:05,315
- Hello.
- Good day.

282
00:17:06,441 --> 00:17:09,611
CEO'S OFFICE

283
00:17:14,282 --> 00:17:17,744
CEO JEONG SEON-HYUK

284
00:17:19,871 --> 00:17:20,872
Yes?

285
00:17:21,998 --> 00:17:23,500
Would you like some coffee, sir?

286
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:25,210
That would be lovely.

287
00:17:36,096 --> 00:17:39,057
MANTUA, ITALY

288
00:18:21,725 --> 00:18:24,644
I'll do everything I can
to set the mood.

289
00:18:24,728 --> 00:18:26,688
- No, don't do anything.
- Yes, sir.

290
00:18:26,771 --> 00:18:28,773
I'll handle Ms. Cha.

291
00:18:28,857 --> 00:18:29,899
Don't worry.

292
00:18:30,233 --> 00:18:33,278
She may seem easy to sway,
but she doesn't open up easily.

293
00:18:34,237 --> 00:18:35,488
I'll lighten the mood somehow.

294
00:18:35,780 --> 00:18:36,906
I'll do my best to back you up.

295
00:18:37,157 --> 00:18:38,867
- Don't. Just stay put.
- Yes, sir. I'll stay put.

296
00:18:39,117 --> 00:18:41,786
Let's give it our all today

297
00:18:41,870 --> 00:18:44,122
and get the best managers
on our side.

298
00:18:47,667 --> 00:18:48,877
ANTACID

299
00:18:56,426 --> 00:18:57,469
You're having one too?

300
00:18:58,386 --> 00:18:59,554
Because we're a team.

301
00:19:49,104 --> 00:19:50,689
- Here they come.
- What?

302
00:19:52,732 --> 00:19:54,359
- Don't be nervous.
- Yes, sir.

303
00:19:55,402 --> 00:19:56,736
- Hey.
- Hello, ladies!

304
00:19:56,820 --> 00:19:58,196
Let me take that for you.

305
00:19:58,279 --> 00:20:01,032
We've been waiting forever
for you ladies.

306
00:20:01,116 --> 00:20:02,617
- Right this way.
- Hello.

307
00:20:02,951 --> 00:20:03,952
Hello.

308
00:20:04,035 --> 00:20:05,954
- Have a seat right here.
- Hello.

309
00:20:06,454 --> 00:20:09,165
When is Hongsung going to hire
some new people?

310
00:20:09,249 --> 00:20:11,209
It's always the same faces.

311
00:20:11,292 --> 00:20:13,002
All old and worn-out.

312
00:20:13,086 --> 00:20:14,421
That's harsh, Ms. Cha.

313
00:20:14,504 --> 00:20:15,880
I'm still in my twenties.

314
00:20:15,964 --> 00:20:17,674
No, you're definitely not.

315
00:20:17,757 --> 00:20:19,592
I swear I am.

316
00:20:19,676 --> 00:20:21,052
No, I don't believe you.

317
00:20:21,136 --> 00:20:23,012
- Just pour us some drinks.
- Thank you.

318
00:20:23,096 --> 00:20:25,265
All right, give me your glasses.

319
00:20:48,788 --> 00:20:49,873
Delicious, isn't it?

320
00:20:58,047 --> 00:21:00,175
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

321
00:21:00,258 --> 00:21:02,761
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

322
00:21:04,345 --> 00:21:05,597
Laknes?

323
00:21:06,806 --> 00:21:08,683
Didn't they go out of business?

324
00:21:08,767 --> 00:21:10,518
You've got it all wrong.

325
00:21:10,602 --> 00:21:14,189
They strategically decided to wait
for the market to peak.

326
00:21:14,522 --> 00:21:15,774
That's called going out of business.

327
00:21:16,065 --> 00:21:17,358
It's true. They did.

328
00:21:17,650 --> 00:21:19,861
But market trends
are always changing.

329
00:21:19,944 --> 00:21:22,113
Now is the right time
for Laknes to make a comeback.

330
00:21:23,990 --> 00:21:24,991
Exactly.

331
00:21:25,074 --> 00:21:27,076
Fine, let's say
they went out of business.

332
00:21:27,160 --> 00:21:29,037
They already failed once.

333
00:21:29,120 --> 00:21:31,247
Would they try again without a plan?

334
00:21:31,331 --> 00:21:34,584
They prepared thoroughly
for their comeback.

335
00:21:35,168 --> 00:21:38,087
Being prepared is great and all

336
00:21:38,171 --> 00:21:40,381
but Ms. Cha recently...

337
00:21:42,258 --> 00:21:43,760
Can I tell them?

338
00:21:44,010 --> 00:21:45,762
Of course not.

339
00:21:45,845 --> 00:21:47,388
- I shouldn't.
- What is it?

340
00:21:47,722 --> 00:21:49,140
So the thing is

341
00:21:49,599 --> 00:21:50,934
she got an offer from a certain brand

342
00:21:51,017 --> 00:21:54,145
to run their flagship store
in Seongsu-dong.

343
00:21:55,772 --> 00:21:56,856
Habsburg?

344
00:21:57,482 --> 00:21:59,359
How did you...

345
00:21:59,442 --> 00:22:01,694
Of course, I know everything
that happens in this industry.

346
00:22:02,779 --> 00:22:03,947
But that place is...

347
00:22:04,572 --> 00:22:05,990
Sure, it's nice.

348
00:22:06,074 --> 00:22:07,826
We can't stop you from going there.

349
00:22:08,368 --> 00:22:11,746
Don't they offer managers
a 15% commission?

350
00:22:11,830 --> 00:22:13,957
I'm sure that's true
for the first month.

351
00:22:14,040 --> 00:22:16,543
But they'll lower it
after their opening month.

352
00:22:16,626 --> 00:22:17,669
I already know.

353
00:22:19,087 --> 00:22:20,171
How do you know?

354
00:22:21,589 --> 00:22:23,967
Those punks always
pull the same scheme.

355
00:22:24,050 --> 00:22:25,051
Ms. Cha.

356
00:22:25,343 --> 00:22:27,136
I wasn't going to say this, but...

357
00:22:31,182 --> 00:22:32,183
Sis.

358
00:22:32,267 --> 00:22:34,394
You're really breaking my heart.

359
00:22:34,769 --> 00:22:35,770
What?

360
00:22:36,855 --> 00:22:38,064
Why are you so naive?

361
00:22:38,940 --> 00:22:41,317
You've been played so many times,
but you still don't get it.

362
00:22:41,401 --> 00:22:43,319
This isn't the first time
they've pulled this.

363
00:22:43,945 --> 00:22:46,531
Why do you keep working with them
when they play you every time?

364
00:22:46,614 --> 00:22:49,033
Why do you always turn us down

365
00:22:49,117 --> 00:22:51,661
and choose to suffer
working with those punks?

366
00:22:51,744 --> 00:22:55,164
I swear I'm not saying this
because you won't work with us.

367
00:22:55,832 --> 00:22:58,251
How many years
have we known each other?

368
00:22:58,334 --> 00:23:01,379
It just breaks my heart
to see you go through that!

369
00:23:01,462 --> 00:23:03,423
Maybe you should stop drinking,
Mr. Yang.

370
00:23:04,090 --> 00:23:06,384
Imagine she were your sister!

371
00:23:07,886 --> 00:23:08,887
Sis.

372
00:23:09,554 --> 00:23:10,638
Just promise me one thing.

373
00:23:12,015 --> 00:23:14,183
I can't force you to work with us

374
00:23:14,601 --> 00:23:17,437
but just don't let them hurt you.

375
00:23:17,854 --> 00:23:20,023
Give it your best shot.

376
00:23:20,690 --> 00:23:22,025
That's all I ask.

377
00:23:26,487 --> 00:23:28,323
Damn, you almost got me.

378
00:23:28,656 --> 00:23:30,450
That was so close.

379
00:23:30,533 --> 00:23:31,910
I thought you were actually drunk.

380
00:23:31,993 --> 00:23:33,953
- We've got a long way to go.
- Oh, my gosh.

381
00:23:34,037 --> 00:23:35,413
- The night is young.
- Jeez.

382
00:23:35,997 --> 00:23:37,373
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

383
00:23:38,875 --> 00:23:40,710
<i>She's so smart</i>

384
00:23:40,793 --> 00:23:42,503
<i>She's so charming</i>

385
00:23:42,587 --> 00:23:45,048
<i>She drives me crazy</i>
<i>I like her so much...</i>

386
00:23:45,131 --> 00:23:46,591
Goodness.

387
00:23:46,966 --> 00:23:48,092
Your glass is empty.

388
00:23:48,176 --> 00:23:49,636
Let me pour you a drink.

389
00:23:50,553 --> 00:23:53,973
I keep drinking,
but I wonder if it's poisoned.

390
00:23:54,057 --> 00:23:56,267
No poison, just sincerity.

391
00:23:56,351 --> 00:23:57,477
Pour me one too.

392
00:23:57,810 --> 00:24:00,271
I can't deal with you, Mr. Yang.

393
00:24:00,355 --> 00:24:01,731
That's too bad. Deal with it.

394
00:24:02,523 --> 00:24:06,027
When we get the Laknes samples,
I'll save you a horsehair bag.

395
00:24:06,861 --> 00:24:09,030
If you're giving me one,
make it alligator.

396
00:24:09,739 --> 00:24:12,116
Alligator is nice too

397
00:24:12,200 --> 00:24:14,118
but you haven't seen
their burgundy horsehair.

398
00:24:14,202 --> 00:24:15,370
It's beautiful.

399
00:24:15,453 --> 00:24:17,080
Horsehair or alligator,
it doesn't matter.

400
00:24:17,163 --> 00:24:18,790
The timing couldn't be worse.

401
00:24:18,873 --> 00:24:20,124
Why did it have to be now?

402
00:24:24,045 --> 00:24:25,088
Do you think it'll work?

403
00:24:28,007 --> 00:24:29,008
I don't know.

404
00:24:29,384 --> 00:24:32,595
Goodness, how can you say that
when you came here to convince me?

405
00:24:33,680 --> 00:24:35,848
I'll be honest with you, Ms. Cha.

406
00:24:35,932 --> 00:24:37,475
I'm not sure about Laknes.

407
00:24:37,725 --> 00:24:40,603
But with you,
I think we can make it work.

408
00:24:41,145 --> 00:24:43,147
Well, aren't you a smooth talker?

409
00:24:43,523 --> 00:24:45,149
Even if it's the same brand

410
00:24:45,233 --> 00:24:48,695
there can be a huge gap in revenue
depending on the manager.

411
00:24:48,778 --> 00:24:49,946
You know that yourself.

412
00:24:50,321 --> 00:24:53,116
I wouldn't ask you
if I didn't believe in this brand.

413
00:24:53,533 --> 00:24:55,743
If anyone could sell it,
then I'd ask anyone.

414
00:24:56,661 --> 00:24:58,830
But this is something
only you can do.

415
00:24:59,747 --> 00:25:02,458
Is that a good thing or a bad thing?

416
00:25:02,542 --> 00:25:04,335
As for incentives and benefits

417
00:25:04,419 --> 00:25:06,713
I'll match the highest
industry standards.

418
00:25:07,171 --> 00:25:09,007
Let's give it a shot, Ms. Cha.

419
00:25:11,092 --> 00:25:12,552
I'm getting played again.

420
00:25:13,302 --> 00:25:14,345
Come on.

421
00:25:14,429 --> 00:25:15,722
Have a drink.

422
00:25:16,848 --> 00:25:17,849
Drink up.

423
00:25:22,353 --> 00:25:26,399
<i>I know you really need me</i>

424
00:25:26,482 --> 00:25:28,401
<i>- You're too perfect</i>
<i>- You're too perfect</i>

425
00:25:28,484 --> 00:25:29,694
<i>- I saw your eyes...</i>
<i>- I saw your eyes...</i>

426
00:25:29,777 --> 00:25:32,739
SINCHON <i>SEOLLEONGTANG</i>

427
00:25:41,539 --> 00:25:43,875
Jeez, those chicks can really drink.

428
00:25:44,959 --> 00:25:46,878
Why say that
after you had such a good time?

429
00:25:47,712 --> 00:25:48,713
Sorry?

430
00:25:50,506 --> 00:25:51,841
It's not right

431
00:25:51,924 --> 00:25:54,385
to bad-mouth people
after having a good time with them.

432
00:25:54,469 --> 00:25:56,262
We're the ones who need them.

433
00:25:57,138 --> 00:25:58,222
Well...

434
00:25:58,306 --> 00:26:00,641
I wasn't exactly bad-mouthing them.

435
00:26:00,725 --> 00:26:04,062
It was more like
an expression of surprise.

436
00:26:04,145 --> 00:26:06,647
Then just say
they can really hold their liquor.

437
00:26:06,731 --> 00:26:09,067
Why are you calling them chicks
and saying they drink too much?

438
00:26:10,485 --> 00:26:12,862
You've been sprouting up lately.

439
00:26:12,945 --> 00:26:14,155
Should I nip that in the bud?

440
00:26:15,448 --> 00:26:16,491
I'm sorry, sir.

441
00:26:18,534 --> 00:26:20,036
- Mr. Yang.
- Thank you.

442
00:26:22,371 --> 00:26:23,956
- Gi-tae.
- Yes, sir.

443
00:26:24,916 --> 00:26:26,250
It's not just you, Gi-tae.

444
00:26:26,334 --> 00:26:27,376
That's human nature.

445
00:26:27,835 --> 00:26:29,462
Everyone's different
behind closed doors.

446
00:26:29,879 --> 00:26:31,130
It's best to be careful.

447
00:26:32,423 --> 00:26:34,008
Yes, sir. I'll keep that in mind.

448
00:26:35,927 --> 00:26:38,721
Don't forget what I said,
even if you go to a new company.

449
00:26:39,555 --> 00:26:40,556
Yes, sir.

450
00:26:41,891 --> 00:26:42,892
Sorry?

451
00:26:43,309 --> 00:26:46,020
So have you made a decision?

452
00:26:46,104 --> 00:26:47,271
Are you leaving the company?

453
00:26:47,730 --> 00:26:48,731
What?

454
00:26:48,981 --> 00:26:50,108
Are you quitting, Park Gi-tae?

455
00:26:51,192 --> 00:26:52,902
What? I mean...

456
00:26:53,444 --> 00:26:54,779
What's with that guilty look?

457
00:26:54,862 --> 00:26:56,114
You did nothing wrong.

458
00:26:56,197 --> 00:26:57,573
I'm just curious.

459
00:26:57,657 --> 00:27:01,077
<i>The luck that passed me by</i>
<i>came together...</i>

460
00:27:01,160 --> 00:27:02,995
- Gi-tae, increase the echo.
- Okay.

461
00:27:03,079 --> 00:27:09,001
<i>It became you and came to me</i>

462
00:27:09,085 --> 00:27:13,089
<i>In a rainstorm</i>

463
00:27:13,381 --> 00:27:14,423
<i>I'll become...</i>

464
00:27:14,507 --> 00:27:16,717
Thank you for the offer, Mr. Gong.

465
00:27:17,218 --> 00:27:18,970
Thank you for seeing me.

466
00:27:19,053 --> 00:27:21,597
But why did you come yourself
this time?

467
00:27:21,681 --> 00:27:23,933
Mr. Yang was always the one
who went drinking with us.

468
00:27:24,308 --> 00:27:27,145
I thought you weren't on good terms
with your team.

469
00:27:27,562 --> 00:27:29,355
I can't say that's entirely false.

470
00:27:29,939 --> 00:27:30,940
Are things better now?

471
00:27:31,566 --> 00:27:34,652
<i>...I'll go anywhere</i>

472
00:27:34,735 --> 00:27:36,737
<i>Trust in me now...</i>

473
00:27:36,821 --> 00:27:39,115
Yes, I'm working on it.

474
00:27:41,742 --> 00:27:44,787
You should work a little harder.

475
00:27:45,997 --> 00:27:46,998
Pardon?

476
00:27:50,209 --> 00:27:53,254
<i>You know Mr. Jeong</i>
<i>started his own business.</i>

477
00:27:55,006 --> 00:27:57,425
<i>Did you know</i>
<i>he's been trying to scout people?</i>

478
00:27:57,800 --> 00:27:59,468
He's much more friendly now.

479
00:28:00,052 --> 00:28:01,220
Really? Mr. Gong?

480
00:28:01,304 --> 00:28:02,471
- Yes.
- No way.

481
00:28:05,433 --> 00:28:08,811
<i>Trust in me now</i>

482
00:28:11,272 --> 00:28:13,149
- Let's go, Laknes!
- Let's go!

483
00:28:14,025 --> 00:28:16,402
I wasn't trying to hide it from you.

484
00:28:16,861 --> 00:28:19,488
But I did get an offer
from Mr. Jeong.

485
00:28:20,031 --> 00:28:23,451
Hey, you should've told us
right away.

486
00:28:24,285 --> 00:28:25,286
I'm sorry, it's just...

487
00:28:25,995 --> 00:28:28,581
I didn't know how to bring it up.

488
00:28:28,664 --> 00:28:29,665
So the thing is...

489
00:28:30,791 --> 00:28:32,043
How do I say this?

490
00:28:32,293 --> 00:28:33,711
I'm not the only one

491
00:28:34,879 --> 00:28:36,964
Mr. Jeong made an offer to.

492
00:28:38,716 --> 00:28:40,218
What are you saying?

493
00:28:41,636 --> 00:28:46,933
He made offers to employees
on other teams as well.

494
00:28:47,433 --> 00:28:48,726
That seemed a bit problematic.

495
00:28:49,227 --> 00:28:51,479
So I was trying to think
of a way to tell you.

496
00:28:53,356 --> 00:28:54,482
As far as I know...

497
00:28:56,150 --> 00:28:57,318
It's more than four people.

498
00:28:59,987 --> 00:29:03,032
What exactly is he trying to do?

499
00:29:06,327 --> 00:29:07,703
<i>What did Ms. Park say?</i>

500
00:29:08,204 --> 00:29:09,664
What do you think?

501
00:29:09,747 --> 00:29:11,791
I said I was quitting,
and she said okay.

502
00:29:13,000 --> 00:29:15,044
Maybe she thought it was inevitable.

503
00:29:15,127 --> 00:29:16,712
She might've even felt grateful.

504
00:29:17,213 --> 00:29:18,214
Hey.

505
00:29:18,422 --> 00:29:19,757
I have to move aside

506
00:29:19,840 --> 00:29:21,968
so people like you
can move up the ladder.

507
00:29:24,637 --> 00:29:27,056
If you resign, where will you go?

508
00:29:30,184 --> 00:29:32,728
You're going to quit at 40
without a plan?

509
00:29:33,437 --> 00:29:34,939
Does your wife know?

510
00:29:35,022 --> 00:29:36,524
Of course, she does.

511
00:29:36,607 --> 00:29:37,858
She told me to do whatever I want.

512
00:29:38,442 --> 00:29:40,569
But she said she'd kill me
if I can't support the family.

513
00:29:48,661 --> 00:29:49,829
Don't you have regrets?

514
00:29:50,204 --> 00:29:51,372
Yes, I do.

515
00:29:52,999 --> 00:29:55,209
Sometimes, I wonder
if I should've worked harder.

516
00:29:55,293 --> 00:29:56,419
If I had

517
00:29:57,128 --> 00:29:59,255
could I have been
a candidate for associate director?

518
00:29:59,338 --> 00:30:00,339
That sort of thing.

519
00:30:01,048 --> 00:30:02,049
Mr. Jeong.

520
00:30:03,259 --> 00:30:05,594
If you just get through
this promotion cycle

521
00:30:05,678 --> 00:30:07,096
I think you'll have a shot.

522
00:30:08,097 --> 00:30:09,098
Hey.

523
00:30:09,515 --> 00:30:11,225
You're skilled

524
00:30:11,309 --> 00:30:14,061
and gaining good work experience,
so you might not know this.

525
00:30:14,437 --> 00:30:16,897
But I wasn't promoted to team leader
based on my skills.

526
00:30:16,981 --> 00:30:18,149
It was based on seniority.

527
00:30:19,275 --> 00:30:22,486
Do you know the highest position
you can reach through seniority?

528
00:30:23,612 --> 00:30:24,905
Team leader.

529
00:30:24,989 --> 00:30:26,115
I'm a team leader.

530
00:30:26,490 --> 00:30:27,491
It's over for me.

531
00:30:30,036 --> 00:30:31,912
Aren't you thinking too negatively?

532
00:30:31,996 --> 00:30:33,622
You're the best at this job.

533
00:30:33,706 --> 00:30:34,915
What are you talking about?

534
00:30:35,833 --> 00:30:36,917
Thanks for saying that.

535
00:30:37,001 --> 00:30:38,002
Jeez.

536
00:30:42,381 --> 00:30:43,382
Eun-tae.

537
00:30:44,216 --> 00:30:45,259
Someday

538
00:30:46,135 --> 00:30:49,221
if we ever meet again through work

539
00:30:50,389 --> 00:30:52,058
I hope you won't be
too disappointed in me.

540
00:30:53,225 --> 00:30:54,643
What are you saying?

541
00:30:54,727 --> 00:30:55,895
I'm just saying.

542
00:30:55,978 --> 00:30:57,521
I hope you don't feel that way.

543
00:31:16,290 --> 00:31:18,334
INCOMING CALL
TEAM 4 MR. JEONG SEON-HYUK

544
00:31:21,921 --> 00:31:25,299
ASSISTANT MANAGER GONG EUN-TAE

545
00:31:25,383 --> 00:31:26,759
<i>- Hello?</i>
- Hey, Eun-tae.

546
00:31:27,009 --> 00:31:28,094
Did you eat dinner?

547
00:31:28,511 --> 00:31:29,845
<i>Why are you doing this?</i>

548
00:31:30,846 --> 00:31:32,181
What are you referring to?

549
00:31:32,681 --> 00:31:34,975
Not showing up to work
after resigning

550
00:31:35,226 --> 00:31:37,019
<i>or poaching employees?</i>

551
00:31:37,436 --> 00:31:38,437
Both, I suppose.

552
00:31:41,190 --> 00:31:43,025
<i>Well, once I thought about it</i>

553
00:31:43,526 --> 00:31:45,611
I realized I couldn't fake a smile
and say goodbye

554
00:31:45,694 --> 00:31:47,822
when I'm betraying everyone.

555
00:31:48,614 --> 00:31:50,241
That's why I haven't been to work.

556
00:31:50,908 --> 00:31:52,785
And it's true that I made job offers.

557
00:31:53,285 --> 00:31:54,829
<i>They can make their own decisions.</i>

558
00:31:54,912 --> 00:31:57,498
So did you just call me
to ask if I had dinner?

559
00:31:59,834 --> 00:32:02,128
So what is Hongsung going to do?

560
00:32:03,629 --> 00:32:05,631
They'll have to punish me somehow.

561
00:32:06,882 --> 00:32:08,426
What exactly are you expecting?

562
00:32:09,135 --> 00:32:11,220
I'm sure you're not far off.

563
00:32:11,929 --> 00:32:13,055
Is that right?

564
00:32:14,265 --> 00:32:15,349
What about you?

565
00:32:16,016 --> 00:32:17,184
Will you stay at Hongsung?

566
00:32:21,939 --> 00:32:23,774
- What do you mean?
<i>- Do you know</i>

567
00:32:24,483 --> 00:32:26,902
what they all say
when I offer them a job?

568
00:32:27,695 --> 00:32:29,613
They thank me
for recognizing their worth.

569
00:32:30,197 --> 00:32:32,616
Hongsung doesn't know
how to develop its employees.

570
00:32:32,992 --> 00:32:34,910
<i>I mean, they have a guy like you</i>

571
00:32:34,994 --> 00:32:37,621
<i>caught up in office politics</i>
<i>and doing odd jobs.</i>

572
00:32:38,080 --> 00:32:41,125
So why don't you take this chance
to think about it?

573
00:32:43,085 --> 00:32:44,587
<i>I'll pretend we never had</i>
<i>this conversation.</i>

574
00:32:48,257 --> 00:32:50,468
HONGSUNG SALES DIVISION 1
TEAM LEADER JEONG SEON-HYUK

575
00:32:50,551 --> 00:32:51,552
Eun-tae.

576
00:32:52,678 --> 00:32:54,513
You're the reason I'm leaving.

577
00:32:55,347 --> 00:32:57,141
<i>I made this decision because of you.</i>

578
00:33:00,769 --> 00:33:06,025
<i>All I did was find the courage</i>
<i>to do the job I'd been given.</i>

579
00:33:07,359 --> 00:33:12,490
<i>I had no idea that courage</i>
<i>would lead to this result.</i>

580
00:33:12,990 --> 00:33:14,074
You see...

581
00:33:15,451 --> 00:33:16,702
I think...

582
00:33:19,455 --> 00:33:21,165
I'll become Hongsung's enemy.

583
00:33:22,583 --> 00:33:25,294
<i>You could say the one</i>
<i>who made him Hongsung's enemy...</i>

584
00:33:27,463 --> 00:33:28,797
<i>was me.</i>

585
00:33:38,516 --> 00:33:40,267
- Good morning.
- Hello, Mr. Gong.

586
00:33:41,101 --> 00:33:42,937
- Hello.
- Hello.

587
00:33:43,604 --> 00:33:45,439
- Hello.
- Hello, sir.

588
00:33:45,940 --> 00:33:47,024
Hello.

589
00:33:47,107 --> 00:33:49,527
- You're here early, Ms. Jang.
- Hello, Mr. Gong.

590
00:33:49,610 --> 00:33:51,111
Good morning, Mr. Gong.

591
00:34:01,288 --> 00:34:04,041
What's going on between you two?

592
00:34:04,458 --> 00:34:05,459
Look at this.

593
00:34:09,046 --> 00:34:10,422
Didn't she do a great job?

594
00:34:10,506 --> 00:34:12,299
Ji-hye worked very hard on it.

595
00:34:12,925 --> 00:34:15,261
You didn't stay up all night
for this, did you?

596
00:34:16,762 --> 00:34:17,763
Please tell me you didn't.

597
00:34:19,390 --> 00:34:20,391
I'm sorry, Ms. Jang.

598
00:34:20,891 --> 00:34:24,228
Tell me if anything is missing
or needs to be revised.

599
00:34:24,311 --> 00:34:25,688
I'll fix it right away.

600
00:34:26,480 --> 00:34:27,982
What I'm trying to say is...

601
00:34:33,112 --> 00:34:34,363
Ji-hye.

602
00:34:35,030 --> 00:34:36,782
Do you have the original file?

603
00:34:37,116 --> 00:34:40,035
Yes, I shared it
on the company network.

604
00:34:40,411 --> 00:34:41,495
That's great.

605
00:34:41,579 --> 00:34:44,039
Let's use it as our team's manual.

606
00:34:44,915 --> 00:34:45,916
Sorry?

607
00:34:47,084 --> 00:34:48,627
I'm really sorry, Ji-hye.

608
00:34:48,711 --> 00:34:50,254
I should have been clearer.

609
00:34:51,171 --> 00:34:54,008
I was just asking
for a simple document

610
00:34:54,091 --> 00:34:56,176
so I could begin working right away.

611
00:34:56,260 --> 00:34:58,387
I wasn't asking you
to write a full report.

612
00:34:59,680 --> 00:35:01,140
It's not like I'm a director.

613
00:35:01,223 --> 00:35:03,183
I mean, this is flawless.

614
00:35:04,226 --> 00:35:06,020
Even I can't make
something like this.

615
00:35:09,064 --> 00:35:13,110
I was going to tell her,
but she was doing such a good job.

616
00:35:13,193 --> 00:35:14,778
I wanted to see the final result...

617
00:35:17,698 --> 00:35:18,699
Ji-hye?

618
00:35:22,786 --> 00:35:23,871
I'm sorry.

619
00:35:25,164 --> 00:35:26,999
I don't know what's wrong with me.

620
00:35:30,085 --> 00:35:31,337
I'm sorry.

621
00:35:37,801 --> 00:35:39,428
I bet you've never been up here.

622
00:35:40,054 --> 00:35:41,096
No, I haven't.

623
00:35:42,222 --> 00:35:44,600
I didn't even know
we had a place like this.

624
00:35:46,727 --> 00:35:47,728
I'm sorry.

625
00:35:48,479 --> 00:35:50,481
I'm sorry
I didn't bring you here sooner

626
00:35:50,564 --> 00:35:52,858
especially after you've been here
for over four months.

627
00:35:53,942 --> 00:35:57,321
And as your team leader,
I didn't know how anxious you were.

628
00:35:57,404 --> 00:35:58,614
I'm also sorry for that.

629
00:35:59,365 --> 00:36:02,826
I loved seeing how hard you worked,
so I left you alone.

630
00:36:03,911 --> 00:36:05,496
I had no clue it was out of anxiety.

631
00:36:08,248 --> 00:36:10,709
You're a contract worker
who has just one year

632
00:36:10,793 --> 00:36:12,920
to prove yourself
if you want to stay here.

633
00:36:13,003 --> 00:36:14,254
It must be tough.

634
00:36:15,172 --> 00:36:17,424
Well, I'm not the only one
in that position.

635
00:36:18,717 --> 00:36:20,260
I can do a better job.

636
00:36:21,679 --> 00:36:23,138
What exactly can you do better,
and how?

637
00:36:24,390 --> 00:36:25,391
I'll be honest.

638
00:36:26,850 --> 00:36:28,143
I can't tell you

639
00:36:29,645 --> 00:36:32,314
to trust me and follow my lead,
or that hard work is all you need.

640
00:36:33,732 --> 00:36:34,858
But instead

641
00:36:35,275 --> 00:36:37,528
I'll do everything I can
to deliver results

642
00:36:37,611 --> 00:36:39,613
starting with Laknes.

643
00:36:40,489 --> 00:36:43,117
If the team gets good results,
I'll gain leverage as team leader.

644
00:36:43,492 --> 00:36:46,161
Then I'll have the confidence
to advocate for you

645
00:36:46,245 --> 00:36:51,375
because Sales Team 5 needs you,
no matter what.

646
00:37:02,261 --> 00:37:03,595
What is this?

647
00:37:04,221 --> 00:37:05,764
It's the file you worked on.

648
00:37:06,432 --> 00:37:07,433
Keep it in your wallet.

649
00:37:08,475 --> 00:37:09,893
Regardless of the outcome

650
00:37:11,061 --> 00:37:14,773
it doesn't change your worth
as the person who made this.

651
00:37:16,191 --> 00:37:17,985
Don't put your faith in the company.

652
00:37:18,694 --> 00:37:20,028
Don't put your faith in me, either.

653
00:37:20,446 --> 00:37:23,574
Trust in your own worth
as the creator of that file.

654
00:37:28,328 --> 00:37:30,330
Thank you, Mr. Gong.

655
00:37:33,959 --> 00:37:35,210
Stay up here a little longer.

656
00:37:35,753 --> 00:37:37,296
Just don't stay here all day.

657
00:37:41,633 --> 00:37:42,634
Mr. Gong.

658
00:37:43,844 --> 00:37:47,681
If I become a full-time employee,
I'll treat you to a meal.

659
00:37:49,057 --> 00:37:50,058
No.

660
00:37:51,477 --> 00:37:52,686
I'll treat you.

661
00:37:53,604 --> 00:37:55,564
I promise I'll buy you
something delicious!

662
00:37:56,148 --> 00:37:57,274
Make it premium Korean beef.

663
00:37:59,276 --> 00:38:00,277
All right.

664
00:38:19,546 --> 00:38:21,006
I'm sorry, Mr. Gong.

665
00:38:21,089 --> 00:38:22,424
I should've made
my instructions clearer.

666
00:38:23,634 --> 00:38:25,844
It was ultimately my mistake.

667
00:38:25,928 --> 00:38:27,012
Don't worry about it.

668
00:38:31,391 --> 00:38:32,392
Mr. Gong.

669
00:38:33,477 --> 00:38:35,604
I'm sure you have
many questions for me.

670
00:38:36,647 --> 00:38:37,981
Why haven't you asked me anything?

671
00:38:40,108 --> 00:38:41,944
If you had something to tell me,
you would've already.

672
00:38:43,028 --> 00:38:46,114
The fact that you haven't
means you're not ready yet.

673
00:38:48,784 --> 00:38:50,786
It wasn't an easy decision for me.

674
00:38:52,746 --> 00:38:54,748
Please just know that.

675
00:39:04,925 --> 00:39:06,260
<i>How many people in total?</i>

676
00:39:06,885 --> 00:39:08,762
Five, as far as we can tell.

677
00:39:08,846 --> 00:39:10,556
Team 1's Park Jin-u,
Team 2's Choi Ju-hui

678
00:39:10,639 --> 00:39:13,517
Team 3's Kang Yeong-seo,
Team 5's Park Gi-tae

679
00:39:14,226 --> 00:39:15,853
and Team 4's Oh Jeong-hyeon.

680
00:39:17,896 --> 00:39:19,648
He tried to completely
dismantle Team 4.

681
00:39:21,400 --> 00:39:22,651
- Mr. Oh.
- Yes, ma'am.

682
00:39:22,734 --> 00:39:23,861
I rejected him right away.

683
00:39:24,486 --> 00:39:26,363
Mr. Jeong didn't clock in
today, either?

684
00:39:27,239 --> 00:39:29,032
He also stopped taking our calls
since yesterday.

685
00:39:29,116 --> 00:39:30,117
I did some digging.

686
00:39:30,200 --> 00:39:33,287
He appears to be mainly importing
gray market products from Mantua.

687
00:39:33,620 --> 00:39:36,874
It seems he established contacts
in Mantua before he quit.

688
00:39:37,416 --> 00:39:40,377
He's also already taken
Safilo and Philipp Plein...

689
00:39:43,380 --> 00:39:44,381
Were you aware?

690
00:39:45,632 --> 00:39:47,384
Their sales figures were poor.

691
00:39:48,135 --> 00:39:50,554
It's been a while since they were
mentioned at the meetings.

692
00:39:53,599 --> 00:39:55,309
Why didn't you stop him?

693
00:39:56,351 --> 00:39:57,978
I figured I'd let him have that much.

694
00:39:58,645 --> 00:40:00,772
I couldn't promote him, anyway.

695
00:40:01,315 --> 00:40:03,066
And he needed to find his own path.

696
00:40:04,610 --> 00:40:06,528
But poaching our people is
taking it too far.

697
00:40:09,072 --> 00:40:10,824
- I think...
- Mr. Jang.

698
00:40:10,908 --> 00:40:11,909
Yes, ma'am.

699
00:40:12,659 --> 00:40:13,660
What are your thoughts?

700
00:40:22,252 --> 00:40:25,213
MULTI-BRAND SHOE STORE
PROJECT PROPOSAL

701
00:40:26,089 --> 00:40:27,174
What is this?

702
00:40:27,257 --> 00:40:29,134
A project proposal
for a multi-brand shoe store?

703
00:40:29,217 --> 00:40:33,013
What if we used this
to put some pressure on Mr. Jeong?

704
00:40:39,895 --> 00:40:40,896
Tell me.

705
00:40:42,314 --> 00:40:43,398
Do you want to take this on?

706
00:40:43,815 --> 00:40:45,025
I'd like the company to take it on.

707
00:40:45,692 --> 00:40:47,527
If you propose this
as associate director

708
00:40:47,611 --> 00:40:49,279
it won't just be Team 5's project.

709
00:40:49,363 --> 00:40:51,531
It'll become the entire
Sales Division's project.

710
00:41:00,374 --> 00:41:02,751
We have to break into this market
at some point, anyway.

711
00:41:03,460 --> 00:41:06,797
Even if we sue Mr. Jeong,
we won't gain anything.

712
00:41:07,172 --> 00:41:09,466
And filing a claim against
our Mantua partners will be useless.

713
00:41:09,549 --> 00:41:11,551
"We had no idea.
What do you expect us to do?"

714
00:41:11,635 --> 00:41:12,844
They'll feign ignorance.

715
00:41:13,595 --> 00:41:14,721
And, to be frank...

716
00:41:17,516 --> 00:41:20,227
we can't stop our employees
from wanting to leave.

717
00:41:20,978 --> 00:41:22,521
So I propose

718
00:41:22,771 --> 00:41:25,148
that we take all of Mantua back.

719
00:41:25,774 --> 00:41:29,486
You want to use the shoe supply
to put pressure on Mantua?

720
00:41:30,237 --> 00:41:32,698
Mr. Jeong gets his entire supply
from Mantua.

721
00:41:33,323 --> 00:41:37,494
So I suggest we become a client
Mantua can't afford to lose.

722
00:41:37,577 --> 00:41:39,079
So big that Mr. Jeong can't compete.

723
00:41:39,830 --> 00:41:41,289
We'll put in a supply order

724
00:41:42,749 --> 00:41:45,043
and cut off
Mr. Jeong's entire supply.

725
00:41:47,129 --> 00:41:48,338
Whose idea was this?

726
00:41:49,965 --> 00:41:51,341
It was Mr. Gong's.

727
00:41:57,222 --> 00:41:58,223
Mr. Gong.

728
00:41:59,391 --> 00:42:00,976
Why a multi-brand shoe store?

729
00:42:05,731 --> 00:42:07,983
With clothing or accessories

730
00:42:08,066 --> 00:42:11,862
we also have to worry about hangers,
displays, props, and more.

731
00:42:11,945 --> 00:42:14,239
The downside to shoes is
that the boxes are bulky.

732
00:42:14,322 --> 00:42:17,534
But they're easy to manage
and require less preparation.

733
00:42:17,617 --> 00:42:19,619
There's also less inventory per store

734
00:42:19,703 --> 00:42:21,163
and, after each season

735
00:42:21,246 --> 00:42:23,665
we can send leftovers to outlets,
which is an advantage.

736
00:42:24,833 --> 00:42:26,960
I believe it's a good project.

737
00:42:27,627 --> 00:42:29,463
Are you almost done
prepping the Laknes launch?

738
00:42:30,255 --> 00:42:31,256
Ms. Park.

739
00:42:32,424 --> 00:42:34,468
I came up with this project

740
00:42:35,052 --> 00:42:37,095
but it doesn't mean
only I can take it on.

741
00:42:37,679 --> 00:42:40,640
Even if you give it to another team,
I'll do my best to help out.

742
00:42:40,932 --> 00:42:41,933
Just answer the question.

743
00:42:43,810 --> 00:42:44,811
Yes.

744
00:42:45,395 --> 00:42:47,147
Construction of the store's interior
is complete.

745
00:42:47,689 --> 00:42:49,024
We've also recruited managers.

746
00:42:49,983 --> 00:42:51,234
So can you take this on?

747
00:42:51,943 --> 00:42:53,111
Yes, I can.

748
00:42:54,112 --> 00:42:55,572
- Mr. Jang.
- Yes, ma'am.

749
00:42:55,655 --> 00:42:57,115
Schedule a meeting
with the Finance Team.

750
00:42:57,532 --> 00:43:00,452
- Mr. Gong, resubmit your proposal.
- Yes, ma'am.

751
00:43:00,786 --> 00:43:03,038
- And get ready for a trip to Mantua.
- Okay.

752
00:43:04,206 --> 00:43:05,207
Goodbye, ma'am.

753
00:43:11,254 --> 00:43:12,255
Eun-tae.

754
00:43:13,590 --> 00:43:14,841
You should pace yourself.

755
00:43:15,175 --> 00:43:17,094
At this rate,
you'll leave the rest of us behind.

756
00:43:17,177 --> 00:43:19,763
He's right. If you're going to do
the multi-brand shoe store

757
00:43:19,846 --> 00:43:22,015
you should give us
some of your other brands.

758
00:43:23,100 --> 00:43:25,227
Okay, I'll discuss it with Mr. Jang.

759
00:43:25,310 --> 00:43:28,647
Yes, talk it over
and help Mr. Kim out.

760
00:43:29,523 --> 00:43:30,524
What?

761
00:43:30,899 --> 00:43:33,193
- What's that supposed to mean?
- Sorry?

762
00:43:33,276 --> 00:43:35,570
Who are you to tell him
to help me out?

763
00:43:36,321 --> 00:43:38,907
Why would I take anything
from a junior colleague?

764
00:43:38,990 --> 00:43:40,075
I mean...

765
00:43:40,575 --> 00:43:43,203
Weren't you planning on
taking some of his brands?

766
00:43:43,286 --> 00:43:44,663
Why are you pretending?

767
00:43:45,205 --> 00:43:46,289
Look at this bastard.

768
00:43:46,957 --> 00:43:48,166
Then what about you?

769
00:43:48,250 --> 00:43:50,127
Are you whining
because you couldn't even get scraps?

770
00:43:50,210 --> 00:43:51,545
"Whining"?

771
00:43:52,045 --> 00:43:53,088
Are you serious?

772
00:43:53,380 --> 00:43:56,842
You're the one
snooping around a junior's team

773
00:43:56,925 --> 00:43:58,343
looking for scraps to take.

774
00:43:58,760 --> 00:44:00,971
Has this bastard lost his mind?
Do you want to fight?

775
00:44:01,054 --> 00:44:03,181
Don't call me a bastard.
We're both team leaders.

776
00:44:03,265 --> 00:44:04,683
How dare you call me that?

777
00:44:04,766 --> 00:44:05,976
What are you, an associate director?

778
00:44:06,059 --> 00:44:07,060
Hey!

779
00:44:16,194 --> 00:44:18,280
What a great example you're setting
as team leaders.

780
00:44:19,322 --> 00:44:22,075
Why don't you get back to work
instead of fighting?

781
00:44:22,325 --> 00:44:23,785
Cut the nonsense.

782
00:44:48,393 --> 00:44:54,232
<i>At a company, one person's decision</i>
<i>inevitably affects others.</i>

783
00:44:56,943 --> 00:45:00,655
<i>Everyone here is</i>
<i>both a cause and an effect</i>

784
00:45:01,114 --> 00:45:02,115
<i>of one another.</i>

785
00:45:08,914 --> 00:45:13,835
THE ORDINARY JACKPOT

786
00:45:41,696 --> 00:45:44,824
2,034,320 WON SENT TO LEE JI-HYE
FROM HONGSUNG INTERNATIONAL

787
00:45:58,797 --> 00:45:59,965
Hello.

788
00:46:00,048 --> 00:46:01,091
Yes, hello.

789
00:46:01,383 --> 00:46:03,593
- How much is this?
- It's 32,000 won.

790
00:46:03,677 --> 00:46:05,011
Could you give me a discount?

791
00:46:05,095 --> 00:46:06,846
Hi, ladies.
Can I help you find something?

792
00:46:06,930 --> 00:46:07,931
- This is so pretty.
- This?

793
00:46:08,014 --> 00:46:09,099
If you like it...

794
00:46:17,023 --> 00:46:19,276
Excuse me, do you have that brown one
in another color?

795
00:46:19,985 --> 00:46:20,986
That's the last one we have.

796
00:46:21,987 --> 00:46:23,863
- How much is this?
- It's 60,000 won.

797
00:46:24,447 --> 00:46:25,782
All right, thank you.

798
00:46:31,121 --> 00:46:32,747
- Hello.
- Welcome.

799
00:46:32,831 --> 00:46:33,957
May I try this on?

800
00:46:34,958 --> 00:46:36,209
Thank you.

801
00:46:42,924 --> 00:46:44,009
Thank you.

802
00:46:44,509 --> 00:46:46,136
It looks great on you.

803
00:46:46,219 --> 00:46:47,387
- Do you think so?
- Yeah.

804
00:46:52,475 --> 00:46:54,602
- That one doesn't look good.
- Right?

805
00:46:57,814 --> 00:46:59,482
That one's so pretty on you.

806
00:46:59,566 --> 00:47:00,734
You should get it.

807
00:47:01,151 --> 00:47:02,235
Thank you.

808
00:47:02,319 --> 00:47:05,322
She said that when we first met.

809
00:47:05,405 --> 00:47:07,699
"Get me baseline margins
for the brands we're in charge of.

810
00:47:07,782 --> 00:47:09,868
Customer prices,
customer service manuals..."

811
00:47:10,201 --> 00:47:12,662
You have no idea, right?
But that's not all.

812
00:47:12,746 --> 00:47:15,165
Credit memo logs,
invoice checklists...

813
00:47:15,248 --> 00:47:17,500
She asked me to prepare all of that.

814
00:47:17,584 --> 00:47:19,627
But do you know what's really crazy?

815
00:47:19,711 --> 00:47:21,504
I memorized it all in one shot.

816
00:47:21,588 --> 00:47:24,132
Isn't it?
You know I'm bad at memorization.

817
00:47:24,215 --> 00:47:26,259
Remember when I ran into my ex
on the street

818
00:47:26,343 --> 00:47:28,595
and stuttered like crazy
because I forgot his name?

819
00:47:29,387 --> 00:47:30,972
I don't know. I still don't remember.

820
00:47:31,056 --> 00:47:33,266
But I memorized all of that
in one shot.

821
00:47:33,350 --> 00:47:34,601
Isn't that amazing?

822
00:47:35,518 --> 00:47:37,937
But you can't just memorize
the words.

823
00:47:38,021 --> 00:47:40,648
There's a logical sequence
based on the workflow.

824
00:47:40,732 --> 00:47:42,484
That's how I memorized it.

825
00:47:42,567 --> 00:47:45,028
Can you imagine how nervous I was?

826
00:47:45,320 --> 00:47:48,031
That assistant manager has
such a strong aura.

827
00:47:48,114 --> 00:47:50,575
She looks at you
like she's studying you.

828
00:47:51,618 --> 00:47:54,662
Like a customs officer
looking you over.

829
00:47:54,746 --> 00:47:56,623
So imagine how hard I worked.

830
00:47:56,706 --> 00:47:58,375
I even lost my appetite.

831
00:47:58,458 --> 00:48:01,169
So when I brought her the file,
do you know what she said...

832
00:48:02,087 --> 00:48:03,588
Yes, what is it?

833
00:48:04,422 --> 00:48:05,965
Your boyfriend came?

834
00:48:06,049 --> 00:48:07,884
Okay, let's talk later.

835
00:48:07,967 --> 00:48:09,010
Bye.

836
00:48:14,682 --> 00:48:16,810
But this is the highlight.

837
00:48:17,977 --> 00:48:20,021
She said I did a great job.

838
00:48:23,942 --> 00:48:25,068
Darn it.

839
00:48:29,864 --> 00:48:31,324
Whatever, I did great.

840
00:51:05,270 --> 00:51:07,272
Subtitles by Eunice Kim
